// STORE-PARTITION CENSUS - which tables are billable and which are free.
//
// Run this IDENTICAL query on BOTH portals, then diff the two table lists:
//
//   Defender  (security.microsoft.com > Hunting > Advanced hunting)
//       -> returns Defender XDR lake tables AND, once the workspace is onboarded to
//          the unified platform, Log Analytics workspace tables. One pane, two stores.
//   Azure     (Microsoft Sentinel > law-soc-lab > Logs, KQL mode)
//       -> returns ONLY the Log Analytics workspace.
//
//   In the Azure list  = workspace-resident = METERED, counts against the daily cap.
//   Dropped from it    = Defender XDR-native = FREE, no matter how large.
//
// This answers a cost question by measurement instead of inference, costs nothing,
// and repeats on demand. Volume in the Defender run is NOT evidence of spend - the
// largest table in the 2026-07-26 census (GraphAPIAuditEvents, 3578 events in 24h)
// bills nothing at all.
//
// Measured 2026-07-26:
//   workspace : SecurityEvent, Heartbeat, Usage, AzureActivity, SigninLogs
//   XDR only  : GraphAPIAuditEvents, EntraIdSignInEvents, EntraIdSpnSignInEvents,
//               EmailEvents, EmailUrlInfo, IdentityInfo
//
// TIMEZONE: the two portals rendered the same rows 7 hours apart - Defender in local
// time, Azure in UTC with the column labelled "Latest [UTC]". Compare offsets, not
// wall clocks. The unlabelled column is the local one.
search *
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| summarize Events = count(), Latest = max(TimeGenerated) by $table
| order by Events desc

// Then, in the AZURE run only, put numbers on the billable half. Usage lags several
// hours, so treat the most recent window as not-yet-reported rather than as zero.
// Usage
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
// | where IsBillable == true
// | summarize BillableMB = sum(Quantity) by DataType
// | order by BillableMB desc
